    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d392">

                <pb facs="0416" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg406"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Spain/1305: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hayes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-27T00:00:00-04:00">April 27,
                            1944—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1182. I refer to Dunn’s conversation with Beaulac and to your 1432, April 25, 7
                    p.m. I endorse your suggestion that you carry this matter to Franco in a final
                    effort to obtain Spanish approval of the proposal contained in our 936, April 4.
                    I feel that you should do this at the earliest possible moment. In the event
                    that Franco still maintains in spite of your direct approach to him that Spain
                    will not accept the proposal outlined in our 936 you are authorized to reach an
                    immediate settlement on the basis of our 1153, April 25, 11 p.m. Your
                    assumptions as to oil provision in your 1450 April 27, are correct. I should not
                    wish any publicity or public announcements regarding a settlement to be made
                    before Wednesday<anchor n="20" xml:id="d392-f1"/> or Thursday of next week.</p>
                <p>I wish to inform you in connection with the press release referred to in my 1154,
                    April 25, midnight,<anchor n="21" xml:id="d392-f2"/> that because of our
                    situation here I must include in any press release a statement to the effect
                    that we have arrived at this settlement at the request of the British Government
                    whose supply situation in Spain differs from ours. Exact text will be cabled
                    later.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
